1
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:13,650
You need to drink, child.

2
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:18,790
And eat.

3
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:25,050
Isn't there anything else?

4
00:02:26,810 --> 00:02:29,620
The Dothraki have two things in abundance:

5
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:33,670
Grass and horses. People can't live on grass.

6
00:02:42,510 --> 00:02:44,900
In the Shadow Lands beyond Asshai,

7
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:47,200
they say there are fields of ghost grass

8
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:50,470
with stalks as pale as milk that glow in the night.

9
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:53,210
It murders all other grass.

10
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:55,770
The Dothraki believe that one day

11
00:02:55,770 --> 00:02:58,990
it will cover everything-- that's the way the world will end.

12
00:03:12,690 --> 00:03:14,310
It'll get easier.

13
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:53,170
Khaleesi!

14
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:54,740
Your hands.

15
00:04:06,130 --> 00:04:08,720
We're still not far from Pentos, your Grace.

16
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:11,640
Magister Illyrio has extended his hospitality.

17
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,180
You'd be more comfortable there.

18
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:15,930
I have no interest in hospitality or comfort.

19
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:17,460
I'll stay with Drogo

20
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:20,770
until he fulfills his end of the bargain and I have my crown.

21
00:04:20,770 --> 00:04:22,330
As you wish, your Grace.

22
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:26,100
Well, Mormont, as brutish as this life is,

23
00:04:26,130 --> 00:04:28,410
I suppose it is preferable to beheading.

24
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:32,090
What did Ned Stark want you for?

25
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:35,170
Buying from a slaver?

26
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:37,350
Selling to one--

27
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:40,280
some poachers I caught on my land.

28
00:04:41,570 --> 00:04:44,690
Under my reign, you won't be punished for such nonsense.

29
00:04:45,110 --> 00:04:47,000
You can rest assured of that.

30
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:14,710
Better-looking bitches than you're used to, Uncle.

31
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,740
My mother's been looking for you.

32
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:23,310
We ride for King's Landing today.

33
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:26,760
Before you go, you will call on Lord and Lady Stark

34
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:28,550
and offer your sympathies.

35
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:31,640
What good will my sympathies do them?

36
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:36,430
None. But it is expected of you.

37
00:05:36,430 --> 00:05:38,170
Your absence has already been noted.

38
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:39,990
The boy means nothing to me.

39
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:42,860
And I can't stand the wailing of women.

40
00:05:45,110 --> 00:05:46,880
One word and I'll hit you again.

41
00:05:46,910 --> 00:05:48,680
I'm telling mother!

42
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:52,450
Go! Tell her.

43
00:05:52,450 --> 00:05:54,600
But first you will get to Lord and Lady Stark

44
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,320
and you will fall on your knees in front of them

45
00:05:56,350 --> 00:05:58,230
and tell them how very sorry you are,

46
00:05:58,230 --> 00:05:59,600
that you are at their service,

47
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:02,690
and that all your prayers are with them. Do you understand?

48
00:06:02,730 --> 00:06:03,860
You can't--

49
00:06:04,930 --> 00:06:06,680
Do you understand?

50
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,750
The prince will remember that, little lord.

51
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,320
I hope so.

52
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:21,020
If he forgets, be a good dog and remind him.

53
00:06:23,910 --> 00:06:27,440
Ah. Time for breakfast.

54
00:06:34,290 --> 00:06:36,740
Bread. And two of those little fish.

55
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:40,940
And a mug of dark beer to wash it down.

56
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:45,730
And bacon, burned black.

57
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:50,620
- Little brother. - Beloved siblings.

58
00:06:54,710 --> 00:06:56,730
Is Bran going to die?

59
00:06:58,570 --> 00:06:59,770
Apparently not.

60
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,660
What do you mean?

61
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,600
The Maester says the boy may live.

62
00:07:14,710 --> 00:07:17,430
It's no mercy, letting a child linger in such pain.

63
00:07:17,470 --> 00:07:19,310
Only the gods know for certain.

64
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:21,880
All the rest of us can do is pray.

65
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:26,130
The charms of the north seem entirely lost on you.

66
00:07:26,130 --> 00:07:27,790
I still can't believe you're going.

67
00:07:27,790 --> 00:07:29,720
It's ridiculous even for you.

68
00:07:29,850 --> 00:07:31,990
Where's your sense of wonder?

69
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:33,600
The greatest structure ever built,

70
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,820
the intrepid men of The Night's Watch,

71
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:38,420
the wintry abode of the White Walkers.

72
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:41,270
Tell me you're not thinking of taking the black.

73
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:43,400
And go celibate?

74
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:46,590
No, the whores would go begging from Dorne to Casterly Rock.

75
00:07:46,590 --> 00:07:48,910
No, I just want to stand on top of the wall

76
00:07:48,910 --> 00:07:50,930
and piss off the edge of the world.

77
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:54,420
The children don't need to hear your filth.

78
00:07:56,620 --> 00:07:58,340
Come.

79
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:08,380
Even if the boy lives, he'll be a cripple, a grotesque.

80
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:11,450
Give me a good clean death any day.

81
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:15,830
Speaking for the grotesques, I'd have to disagree.

82
00:08:16,210 --> 00:08:19,320
Death is so final, whereas life...

83
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:21,640
Ah, life is full of possibilities.

84
00:08:22,230 --> 00:08:23,730
I hope the boy does wake.

85
00:08:23,770 --> 00:08:26,210
I'd be very interested to hear what he has to say.

86
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:30,840
My dear brother,

87
00:08:31,020 --> 00:08:33,830
there are times you make me wonder whose side you're on.

88
00:08:33,830 --> 00:08:36,130
My dear brother, you wound me.

89
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:38,590
You know how much I love my family.

90
00:08:57,960 --> 00:08:59,320
Please.

91
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:02,300
Oh, I would have dressed, your Grace.

92
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:05,150
This is your home. I'm your guest.

93
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:10,090
Handsome one, isn't he?

94
00:09:10,830 --> 00:09:15,160
I lost my first boy, a little black-haired beauty.

95
00:09:15,770 --> 00:09:17,600
He was a fighter too--

96
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:20,030
tried to beat the fever that took him.

97
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:23,350
Forgive me.

98
00:09:24,210 --> 00:09:26,460
It's the last thing you need to hear right now.

99
00:09:26,460 --> 00:09:27,960
I never knew.

100
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:29,780
It was years ago.

101
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:34,840
Robert was crazed, beat his hands bloody on the wall,

102
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:38,150
all the things men do to show you how much they care.

103
00:09:43,460 --> 00:09:45,560
The boy looked just like him.

104
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:49,330
Such a little thing...

105
00:09:50,100 --> 00:09:52,020
A bird without feathers.

106
00:09:54,790 --> 00:09:59,790
They came to take his body away and Robert held me.

107
00:10:00,250 --> 00:10:02,550
I screamed and I battled, but he held me.

108
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:09,540
That little bundle.

109
00:10:11,470 --> 00:10:13,280
They took him away and I never saw him again.

110
00:10:13,310 --> 00:10:16,060
Never have visited the crypt, never.

111
00:10:26,790 --> 00:10:28,290
I pray to the mother every morning and night

112
00:10:28,330 --> 00:10:30,950
that she return your child to you.

113
00:10:32,830 --> 00:10:34,570
I am grateful.

114
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:37,360
Perhaps this time she'll listen.

115
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:31,490
A sword for the wall?

116
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:35,580
- I already have one. - Good man.

117
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:38,630
- Have you swung it yet? - Of course I have.

118
00:11:38,930 --> 00:11:40,660
At someone, I mean.

119
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:47,970
It's a strange thing, the first time you cut a man.

120
00:11:48,570 --> 00:11:51,460
You realize we're nothing but sacks of meat and blood

121
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,220
and some bone to keep it all standing.

122
00:11:57,190 --> 00:11:59,020
Let me thank you ahead of time

123
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:02,090
for guarding us all from the perils beyond the wall--

124
00:12:02,090 --> 00:12:04,620
Wildlings and White Walkers and whatnot.

125
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:11,180
We're grateful to have good, strong men like you protecting us.

126
00:12:13,390 --> 00:12:15,990
We've guarded the kingdoms for 8,000 years.

127
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:21,580
Is it "we" already?

128
00:12:22,510 --> 00:12:24,170
Have you taken your vows then?

129
00:12:24,210 --> 00:12:25,600
Soon enough.

130
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:30,250
Give my regards to The Night's Watch.

131
00:12:30,630 --> 00:12:33,520
I'm sure it will be thrilling to serve in such an elite force.

132
00:12:33,550 --> 00:12:35,200
And if not?

133
00:12:35,950 --> 00:12:37,770
It's only for life.

134
00:12:57,430 --> 00:12:59,090
Thank you, Nymeria.

135
00:13:06,690 --> 00:13:09,160
Septa Mordane says I have to do it again.

136
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:11,850
My things weren't properly folded, she says.

137
00:13:12,050 --> 00:13:13,260
Who cares how they're folded?!

138
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:15,300
They're going to get all messed up anyway.

139
00:13:15,890 --> 00:13:17,030
It's good you've got help.

140
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:18,690
Watch.

141
00:13:18,930 --> 00:13:21,360
Nymeria, gloves.

142
00:13:27,320 --> 00:13:29,350
- Impressive. - Shut up.

143
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:32,240
Nymeria, gloves!

144
00:13:33,750 --> 00:13:35,640
I have something for you.

145
00:13:35,850 --> 00:13:38,320
And it has to be packed very carefully.

146
00:13:38,750 --> 00:13:40,110
A present?

147
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:41,420
Close the door.

148
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:56,170
This is no toy.

149
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:02,300
Be careful you don't cut yourself.

150
00:14:05,140 --> 00:14:07,390
- It's so skinny. - So are you.

151
00:14:08,630 --> 00:14:10,880
I had the blacksmith make it for you special.

152
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:12,000
It won't hack a man's head off,

153
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,820
but it can poke him full of holes if you're quick enough.

154
00:14:13,850 --> 00:14:14,890
I can be quick.

155
00:14:14,910 --> 00:14:17,000
You'll have to work at it every day.

156
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:19,700
How does it feel?

157
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:22,090
Do you like the balance?

158
00:14:22,990 --> 00:14:24,480
I think so.

159
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:28,480
First lesson: Stick them with the pointy end.

160
00:14:28,670 --> 00:14:30,690
I know which end to use.

161
00:14:36,190 --> 00:14:37,970
I'm going to miss you.

162
00:14:39,310 --> 00:14:40,880
Careful.

163
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:54,450
All the best swords have names, you know.

164
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:00,780
Sansa can keep her sewing needles.

165
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:04,170
I've got a needle of my own.

166
00:15:18,970 --> 00:15:21,140
I came to say goodbye to Bran.

167
00:15:21,140 --> 00:15:22,920
You've said it.

168
00:15:33,820 --> 00:15:36,310
I wish I could be here when you wake up.

169
00:15:39,540 --> 00:15:41,830
I'm going north with Uncle Benjen.

170
00:15:42,250 --> 00:15:44,070
I'm taking the black.

171
00:15:52,780 --> 00:15:55,790
I know we always talked about seeing the wall together,

172
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:57,310
but you'll be able to come visit me

173
00:15:57,310 --> 00:15:59,300
at Castle Black when you're better.

174
00:16:01,020 --> 00:16:03,310
I'll know my way around by then.

175
00:16:03,740 --> 00:16:06,330
I'll be a sworn brother of The Night's Watch.

176
00:16:11,310 --> 00:16:14,400
We can go out walking beyond the wall, if you're not afraid.

177
00:16:29,380 --> 00:16:33,790
I want you to leave.

178
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:37,790
17 years ago you rode off with Robert Baratheon.

179
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:43,460
You came back a year later with another woman's son.

180
00:17:44,910 --> 00:17:47,290
And now you're leaving again.

181
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,860
I have no choice.

182
00:17:51,860 --> 00:17:55,200
That's what men always say when honor calls.

183
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:59,110
That's what you tell your families, tell yourselves.

184
00:18:00,910 --> 00:18:03,580
You do have a choice.

185
00:18:04,350 --> 00:18:06,340
And you've made it.

186
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:12,010
Cat...

187
00:18:17,090 --> 00:18:19,360
I can't do it, Ned.

188
00:18:22,430 --> 00:18:25,790
- I really can't. - You can.

189
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:30,300
You must.

190
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:54,970
You've said goodbye to Bran?

191
00:18:56,100 --> 00:18:57,800
He's not going to die. I know it.

192
00:18:57,830 --> 00:19:00,190
You Starks are hard to kill.

193
00:19:01,370 --> 00:19:02,730
My mother?

194
00:19:02,950 --> 00:19:06,100
- She was very kind. - Good.

195
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:09,800
Next time I see you, you'll be all in black.

196
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:12,190
It was always my color.

197
00:19:13,010 --> 00:19:16,350
- Farewell, Snow. - And you, Stark.

198
00:20:08,730 --> 00:20:10,770
There's great honor serving in The Night's Watch.

199
00:20:13,130 --> 00:20:16,140
The Starks have manned the wall for thousands of years.

200
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:19,810
And you are a Stark.

201
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:21,860
You might not have my name,

202
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:24,440
but you have my blood.

203
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:32,510
Is my mother alive?

204
00:20:33,310 --> 00:20:36,320
Does she know about me? Where I am, where I'm going?

205
00:20:37,860 --> 00:20:39,380
Does she care?

206
00:20:41,060 --> 00:20:43,140
The next time we see each other,

207
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:45,880
we'll talk about your mother.

208
00:20:47,970 --> 00:20:49,620
I promise.

209
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:32,480
Gods, this is country!

210
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:37,750
I've half a mind to leave them all behind and keep going.

211
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:41,950
I've half a mind to go with you.

212
00:21:42,540 --> 00:21:44,100
What do you say, just you and me

213
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:46,700
on the Kingsroad, swords at our sides,

214
00:21:46,890 --> 00:21:50,400
a couple of tavern wenches to warm our beds tonight.

215
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:52,540
You should have asked me 20 years ago.

216
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:56,390
There were wars to fight, women to marry...

217
00:21:56,850 --> 00:21:58,290
we never had the chance to be young.

218
00:21:58,290 --> 00:22:00,250
I recall a few chances.

219
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:06,580
There was that one... Oh, what was her name?

220
00:22:06,760 --> 00:22:08,550
That common girl of yours?

221
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:11,910
Becca? With the great big tits you could bury your face in.

222
00:22:11,910 --> 00:22:14,190
Bessie. She was one of yours.

223
00:22:14,190 --> 00:22:17,520
Bessie! Thank the gods for Bessie

224
00:22:17,520 --> 00:22:19,320
and her tits.

225
00:22:20,370 --> 00:22:22,720
Yours was... Aleena?

226
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:26,060
No. You told me once. Meryl?

227
00:22:26,620 --> 00:22:28,210
Your bastard's mother?

228
00:22:29,690 --> 00:22:32,370
- Wylla. - That's it.

229
00:22:32,370 --> 00:22:33,670
She must have been a rare wench

230
00:22:33,670 --> 00:22:36,960
to make Lord Eddard Stark forget his honor.

231
00:22:37,330 --> 00:22:39,280
You never told me what she looked like.

232
00:22:40,230 --> 00:22:41,750
Nor will I.

233
00:22:44,050 --> 00:22:45,710
We were at war.

234
00:22:45,890 --> 00:22:48,730
None of us knew if we were gonna go back home again.

235
00:22:48,730 --> 00:22:52,770
You're too hard on yourself. You always have been.

236
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:57,830
I swear if I weren't your King, you'd have hit me already.

237
00:22:57,830 --> 00:23:00,010
The worst thing about your coronation...

238
00:23:00,810 --> 00:23:02,890
I'll never get to hit you again.

239
00:23:04,900 --> 00:23:07,680
Trust me, that's not the worst thing.

240
00:23:11,580 --> 00:23:13,600
There was a rider in the night.

241
00:23:19,580 --> 00:23:23,150
Daenerys Targaryen has wed some Dothraki horselord.

242
00:23:23,150 --> 00:23:25,470
What of it? Should we send her a wedding gift?

243
00:23:25,500 --> 00:23:27,620
A knife perhaps, a good sharp one,

244
00:23:27,820 --> 00:23:29,770
and a bold man to wield it.

245
00:23:29,770 --> 00:23:31,690
She's little more than a child.

246
00:23:31,690 --> 00:23:33,990
Soon enough that child will spread her legs

247
00:23:33,990 --> 00:23:35,070
and start breeding.

248
00:23:35,070 --> 00:23:36,690
Tell me we're not speaking of this.

249
00:23:36,690 --> 00:23:38,760
Oh, it's unspeakable to you?

250
00:23:38,950 --> 00:23:42,070
What her father did to your family... that was unspeakable.

251
00:23:42,070 --> 00:23:44,590
What Rhaegar Targaryen did to your sister...

252
00:23:44,590 --> 00:23:46,730
the woman I loved.

253
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:49,940
I'll kill every Targaryen I get my hands on.

254
00:23:49,940 --> 00:23:51,860
But you can't get your hands on this one, can you?

255
00:23:51,890 --> 00:23:53,790
This Khal Drogo,

256
00:23:54,540 --> 00:23:57,040
it's said he has 100,000 men in his horde.

257
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:59,510
Even a million Dothraki are no threat to the realm,

258
00:23:59,510 --> 00:24:02,170
as long as they remain on the other side of the Narrow Sea.

259
00:24:02,170 --> 00:24:03,910
They have no ships, Robert.

260
00:24:03,910 --> 00:24:07,660
There are still those in the Seven Kingdoms who call me usurper.

261
00:24:08,580 --> 00:24:12,220
If the Targaryen boy crosses with a Dothraki horde at his back,

262
00:24:12,410 --> 00:24:15,610
- the scum will join him. - He will not cross.

263
00:24:16,390 --> 00:24:19,720
And if by chance he does, we'll throw him back into the sea.

264
00:24:25,100 --> 00:24:27,180
There's a war coming, Ned.

265
00:24:28,090 --> 00:24:31,070
I don't know when, I don't know who we'll be fighting,

266
00:24:31,440 --> 00:24:33,120
but it's coming.

267
00:25:44,860 --> 00:25:46,190
Sit.

268
00:25:46,870 --> 00:25:48,330
You'll be fed.

269
00:25:52,580 --> 00:25:54,130
Untie them.

270
00:25:55,550 --> 00:25:58,560
Ah, rapers.

271
00:25:59,830 --> 00:26:03,730
They were given a choice no doubt-- castration or the wall.

272
00:26:04,330 --> 00:26:06,540
Most choose the knife.

273
00:26:11,020 --> 00:26:13,670
Not impressed by your new brothers?

274
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:18,370
Lovely thing about the watch--

275
00:26:19,110 --> 00:26:21,970
you discard your old family and get a whole new one.

276
00:26:30,790 --> 00:26:32,570
Why do you read so much?

277
00:26:33,330 --> 00:26:35,560
Look at me and tell me what you see.

278
00:26:37,150 --> 00:26:38,710
Is this a trick?

279
00:26:40,090 --> 00:26:42,710
What you see is a dwarf.

280
00:26:43,090 --> 00:26:44,410
If I'd been born a peasant

281
00:26:44,410 --> 00:26:46,130
they might've left me out in the woods to die.

282
00:26:46,130 --> 00:26:50,070
Alas, I was born a Lannister of Casterly Rock.

283
00:26:50,440 --> 00:26:52,420
Things are expected of me.

284
00:26:52,630 --> 00:26:55,270
My father was the Hand of the King for 20 years.

285
00:26:55,270 --> 00:26:57,370
Until your brother killed that King.

286
00:27:03,130 --> 00:27:06,990
Yes, until my brother killed him.

287
00:27:08,830 --> 00:27:11,390
Life is full of these little ironies.

288
00:27:12,310 --> 00:27:14,570
My sister married the new King

289
00:27:14,570 --> 00:27:17,860
and my repulsive nephew will be King after him.

290
00:27:20,480 --> 00:27:22,430
I must do my part for the honor of my house,

291
00:27:22,430 --> 00:27:23,840
wouldn't you agree?

292
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:27,140
But how?

293
00:27:27,740 --> 00:27:30,050
Well, my brother has his sword

294
00:27:30,250 --> 00:27:31,780
and I have my mind.

295
00:27:31,780 --> 00:27:35,160
And a mind needs books like a sword needs a whetstone.

296
00:27:35,760 --> 00:27:38,550
That's why I read so much, Jon Snow.

297
00:27:42,580 --> 00:27:44,300
And you?

298
00:27:44,300 --> 00:27:46,750
What's your story, bastard?

299
00:27:48,790 --> 00:27:52,120
Ask me nicely and maybe I'll tell you, dwarf.

300
00:27:55,980 --> 00:27:59,100
A bastard boy with nothing to inherit,

301
00:27:59,300 --> 00:28:03,710
off to join the ancient order of The Night's Watch,

302
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:07,210
alongside his Valiant brothers-in-arms.

303
00:28:07,210 --> 00:28:09,020
The Night's Watch protects the realm from...

304
00:28:09,020 --> 00:28:12,390
ah, yes yes, against grumpkins and snarks

305
00:28:12,390 --> 00:28:16,520
and all the other monsters your wet nurse warned you about.

306
00:28:16,520 --> 00:28:18,350
You're a smart boy.

307
00:28:18,350 --> 00:28:20,700
You don't believe that nonsense.

308
00:28:28,660 --> 00:28:31,700
Everything's better with some wine in the belly.

309
00:29:06,100 --> 00:29:09,300
It's time we reviewed the accounts, my lady.

310
00:29:10,040 --> 00:29:13,640
You'll want to know how much this royal visit has cost us.

311
00:29:15,490 --> 00:29:17,290
Talk to Poole about it.

312
00:29:19,570 --> 00:29:22,760
Poole went south with Lord Stark, my lady.

313
00:29:24,050 --> 00:29:25,370
We need a new steward,

314
00:29:25,370 --> 00:29:28,550
and there are several other appointments that require

315
00:29:28,910 --> 00:29:32,520
- our immediate attention-- - I don't care about appointments!

316
00:29:33,770 --> 00:29:35,900
I'll make the appointments.

317
00:29:38,460 --> 00:29:40,710
We'll talk about it first thing in the morning.

318
00:29:40,710 --> 00:29:42,460
Very good, my Lord.

319
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:46,550
My Lady.

320
00:29:59,560 --> 00:30:01,690
When was the last time you left this room?

321
00:30:03,100 --> 00:30:04,540
I have to take care of him.

322
00:30:04,540 --> 00:30:06,170
He's not going to die, mother.

323
00:30:06,170 --> 00:30:08,230
Maester Luwin says the most dangerous time has passed.

324
00:30:08,230 --> 00:30:09,580
What if he's wrong?

325
00:30:09,910 --> 00:30:12,810
- Bran needs me. - Rickon needs you.

326
00:30:13,710 --> 00:30:15,320
He's six.

327
00:30:15,970 --> 00:30:18,980
He doesn't know what's happening. He follows me around all day,

328
00:30:18,980 --> 00:30:21,510
- clutching my leg, crying-- - Close the windows!

329
00:30:21,510 --> 00:30:24,600
I can't stand it! Please make them stop!

330
00:30:27,910 --> 00:30:29,160
Fire.

331
00:30:30,480 --> 00:30:32,480
You stay here. I'll come back.

332
00:30:50,350 --> 00:30:52,350
You're not supposed to be here.

333
00:30:52,440 --> 00:30:54,690
No one is supposed to be here.

334
00:30:55,660 --> 00:30:59,290
It's a mercy. He's dead already.

335
00:31:01,290 --> 00:31:02,410
No!

336
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:14,020
- Have you ever seen a dragon? - Dragon gone, Khaleesi.

337
00:32:14,350 --> 00:32:17,080
Everywhere? Even in the east?

338
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:20,130
No dragon. Brave men kill them.

339
00:32:20,550 --> 00:32:22,910
- It is known. - It is known.

340
00:32:23,690 --> 00:32:27,040
A trader from Qarth told me that dragons come from the moon.

341
00:32:27,230 --> 00:32:28,520
The moon?

342
00:32:29,200 --> 00:32:31,660
He told me the moon was an egg, Khaleesi,

343
00:32:31,950 --> 00:32:34,650
that once there were two moons in the sky.

344
00:32:34,940 --> 00:32:36,260
But one wandered too close

345
00:32:36,260 --> 00:32:38,890
to the sun and it cracked from the heat.

346
00:32:38,890 --> 00:32:41,710
Out of it poured a thousand thousand dragons

347
00:32:41,720 --> 00:32:43,790
and they drank the sun's fire.

348
00:32:44,970 --> 00:32:46,860
Moon is no egg.

349
00:32:46,910 --> 00:32:49,680
Moon is goddess-- wife of sun.

350
00:32:49,750 --> 00:32:52,340
- It is known. - It is known.

351
00:32:54,060 --> 00:32:55,740
Leave me with her.

352
00:33:03,920 --> 00:33:07,020
Why did the trader from Qarth tell you these stories?

353
00:33:07,760 --> 00:33:10,380
Men like to talk when they're happy.

354
00:33:10,450 --> 00:33:12,270
Before your brother bought me for you,

355
00:33:12,270 --> 00:33:14,790
it was my job to make men happy.

356
00:33:15,140 --> 00:33:17,630
- How old were you? - I was nine

357
00:33:17,630 --> 00:33:19,610
when my mother sold me to the pleasure house.

358
00:33:19,610 --> 00:33:20,980
Nine?!

359
00:33:21,880 --> 00:33:24,900
I did not touch a man for three years, Khaleesi.

360
00:33:25,260 --> 00:33:28,620
First you must learn.

361
00:33:31,310 --> 00:33:34,980
Can you teach me how to make the Khal happy?

362
00:33:35,930 --> 00:33:39,730
- Yes. - Will it take three years?

363
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:42,950
No.

364
00:34:04,360 --> 00:34:05,750
Welcome.

365
00:35:36,410 --> 00:35:40,160
What I am about to tell you must remain between us.

366
00:35:41,820 --> 00:35:44,430
I don't think Bran fell from that tower.

367
00:35:46,030 --> 00:35:48,170
I think he was thrown.

368
00:35:49,260 --> 00:35:51,800
The boy was always sure-footed before.

369
00:35:51,800 --> 00:35:54,380
Someone tried to kill him twice.

370
00:35:54,880 --> 00:35:57,910
Why? Why murder an innocent child?

371
00:35:57,910 --> 00:36:00,840
Unless he saw something he wasn't meant to see.

372
00:36:00,840 --> 00:36:03,540
- Saw what, my lady? - I don't know.

373
00:36:04,600 --> 00:36:07,530
But I would stake my life the Lannisters are involved.

374
00:36:07,530 --> 00:36:10,760
We already have reason to suspect their loyalty to the crown.

375
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:12,880
Did you notice the dagger the killer used?

376
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:15,070
It's too fine a weapon for such a man.

377
00:36:15,300 --> 00:36:18,640
The blade is Valyrian steel, the handle dragonbone.

378
00:36:18,750 --> 00:36:20,600
Someone gave it to him.

379
00:36:21,940 --> 00:36:25,680
They come into our home and try to murder my brother?

380
00:36:26,100 --> 00:36:27,280
If it's war they want--

381
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:28,700
If it comes to that, you know I'll stand behind you.

382
00:36:28,700 --> 00:36:32,400
What, is there going to be a battle in the Godswood?

383
00:36:34,660 --> 00:36:37,710
Too easily words of war become acts of war.

384
00:36:37,720 --> 00:36:39,630
We don't know the truth yet.

385
00:36:40,060 --> 00:36:42,510
Lord Stark must be told of this.

386
00:36:42,520 --> 00:36:45,000
I don't trust a raven to carry these words.

387
00:36:45,010 --> 00:36:47,100
- I'll ride to King's Landing. - No.

388
00:36:47,100 --> 00:36:49,800
There must always be a Stark in Winterfell.

389
00:36:50,120 --> 00:36:52,250
- I will go myself. - Mother, you can't.

390
00:36:52,250 --> 00:36:53,720
I must.

391
00:36:54,730 --> 00:36:57,580
I'll send Hal with a squad of guardsmen to escort you.

392
00:36:57,580 --> 00:37:00,220
Too large a party attracts unwanted attention.

393
00:37:00,220 --> 00:37:02,440
I don't want the Lannisters to know I'm coming.

394
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:04,420
Let me accompany you at least.

395
00:37:04,420 --> 00:37:07,430
The Kingsroad can be a dangerous place for a woman alone.

396
00:37:11,270 --> 00:37:12,900
What about Bran?

397
00:37:14,900 --> 00:37:18,230
I have prayed to the Seven for more than a month.

398
00:37:18,910 --> 00:37:22,580
Bran's life is in their hands now.

399
00:38:21,430 --> 00:38:23,130
No, Khaleesi.

400
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:25,980
You must look in his eyes always.

401
00:38:26,530 --> 00:38:28,680
Love comes in at the eyes.

402
00:38:29,900 --> 00:38:33,110
It is said that Irogenia of Lys could finish a man

403
00:38:33,110 --> 00:38:35,310
with nothing but her eyes.

404
00:38:35,310 --> 00:38:36,810
Finish a man?

405
00:38:42,100 --> 00:38:45,740
Kings traveled across the world for a night with Irogenia.

406
00:38:45,740 --> 00:38:48,390
Magisters sold their palaces.

407
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:52,500
Khals burned her enemies just to have her for a few hours.

408
00:38:52,910 --> 00:38:55,980
They say a thousand men proposed to her

409
00:38:55,980 --> 00:38:58,570
and she refused them all.

410
00:38:58,920 --> 00:39:01,510
Well, she sounds like an interesting woman.

411
00:39:02,230 --> 00:39:04,050
I-- I don't think

412
00:39:04,050 --> 00:39:06,530
that Drogo will like it with me on top.

413
00:39:06,530 --> 00:39:09,040
You will make him like it, Khaleesi.

414
00:39:09,170 --> 00:39:11,150
Men want what they've never had.

415
00:39:11,150 --> 00:39:14,690
And the Dothraki take slaves like a hound takes a bitch.

416
00:39:15,810 --> 00:39:18,090
Are you a slave, Khaleesi?

417
00:39:29,070 --> 00:39:31,670
Then don't make love like a slave.

418
00:39:40,340 --> 00:39:41,970
Very good, Khaleesi.

419
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:44,990
Out there he is the mighty Khal,

420
00:39:45,090 --> 00:39:48,440
but in this tent, he belongs to you.

421
00:39:49,100 --> 00:39:50,850
I-- I don't think

422
00:39:50,850 --> 00:39:52,920
that this is the Dothraki way.

423
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:55,790
If he wanted the Dothraki way,

424
00:39:56,310 --> 00:39:58,310
why did he marry you?

425
00:40:47,120 --> 00:40:48,300
No.

426
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:53,420
No!

427
00:42:45,710 --> 00:42:47,270
Pardon me, Ser.

428
00:42:51,060 --> 00:42:52,970
Do I frighten you so much, girl?

429
00:42:54,830 --> 00:42:57,190
Or is it him there making you shake?

430
00:42:58,630 --> 00:43:00,310
He frightens me too.

431
00:43:00,460 --> 00:43:02,130
Look at that face.

432
00:43:03,940 --> 00:43:06,430
I'm sorry if I offended you, Ser.

433
00:43:12,700 --> 00:43:13,750
Why won't he speak to me?

434
00:43:13,750 --> 00:43:16,610
He hasn't been very talkative these last 20 years.

435
00:43:16,910 --> 00:43:19,840
Since the Mad King had his tongue ripped out with hot pincers.

436
00:43:19,840 --> 00:43:22,080
He speaks damn well with his sword though.

437
00:43:22,610 --> 00:43:26,600
Ser Ilyn Payne, the King's Justice.

438
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:29,520
The royal executioner.

439
00:43:31,680 --> 00:43:33,310
What is it, sweet lady?

440
00:43:35,690 --> 00:43:37,460
Does the hound frighten you?

441
00:43:38,220 --> 00:43:39,930
Away with you, dog.

442
00:43:40,490 --> 00:43:42,250
You're scaring my lady.

443
00:43:44,420 --> 00:43:46,120
I don't like to see you upset.

444
00:43:49,200 --> 00:43:50,930
The sun is finally shining.

445
00:43:51,840 --> 00:43:53,360
Come walk with me.

446
00:43:55,040 --> 00:43:56,450
Stay, Lady.

447
00:44:13,700 --> 00:44:15,790
I probably shouldn't have any more.

448
00:44:15,790 --> 00:44:18,190
Father only lets us have one cup at feasts.

449
00:44:18,190 --> 00:44:21,120
My princess can drink as much as she wants.

450
00:44:33,680 --> 00:44:36,560
Don't worry-- you're safe with me.

451
00:44:37,300 --> 00:44:38,380
I'll get you!

452
00:44:44,850 --> 00:44:47,770
- Arya! - Ow!

453
00:44:47,910 --> 00:44:49,500
What are you doing here?

454
00:44:49,730 --> 00:44:51,650
- Go away. - Your sister?

455
00:44:55,420 --> 00:44:58,300
- And who are you, boy? - Mycah, my Lord.

456
00:44:58,300 --> 00:45:01,090
- He the butcher's boy. - He's my friend.

457
00:45:01,090 --> 00:45:04,400
A butcher's boy who wants to be a Knight, eh?

458
00:45:05,450 --> 00:45:07,110
Pick up your sword, butcher's boy.

459
00:45:07,110 --> 00:45:08,940
Let's see how good you are.

460
00:45:08,940 --> 00:45:11,170
She asked me to, my Lord. She asked me to.

461
00:45:11,170 --> 00:45:12,920
I'm your prince,

462
00:45:13,750 --> 00:45:15,010
not your lord,

463
00:45:15,010 --> 00:45:18,780
and I said pick up your sword.

464
00:45:18,780 --> 00:45:20,590
It's not a sword, my prince. It's only a stick.

465
00:45:20,590 --> 00:45:22,730
And you're not a Knight.

466
00:45:24,110 --> 00:45:26,290
Only a butcher's boy.

467
00:45:26,980 --> 00:45:29,660
That was my lady's sister you were hitting, do you know that?

468
00:45:29,660 --> 00:45:32,130
- Stop it! - Arya, stay out of this.

469
00:45:32,540 --> 00:45:34,240
I won't hurt him...

470
00:45:35,260 --> 00:45:36,610
Much.

471
00:45:44,550 --> 00:45:45,670
Arya!

472
00:45:47,210 --> 00:45:48,540
Filthy little bitch!

473
00:45:48,540 --> 00:45:50,510
No no, stop it, stop it, both of you.

474
00:45:50,510 --> 00:45:53,220
You're spoiling it. You're spoiling everything!

475
00:45:54,140 --> 00:45:56,600
I'll gut you, you little cunt!

476
00:45:59,040 --> 00:46:01,210
- Arya! - Nymeria!

477
00:46:01,210 --> 00:46:03,540
- Arya! - Nymeria!

478
00:46:09,010 --> 00:46:10,230
No.

479
00:46:10,770 --> 00:46:13,360
No. Please don't.

480
00:46:13,360 --> 00:46:15,290
Arya, leave him alone.

481
00:46:34,350 --> 00:46:36,150
My prince, my poor prince,

482
00:46:36,150 --> 00:46:37,540
look what they did to you.

483
00:46:37,930 --> 00:46:40,480
Stay here, I'll go back to the inn and bring help.

484
00:46:40,480 --> 00:46:42,050
Then go!

485
00:46:43,520 --> 00:46:45,170
Don't touch me.

486
00:46:47,870 --> 00:46:50,870
The wolf's not here. Look down by the stream.

487
00:46:56,850 --> 00:47:00,430
You've got to go. They'll kill you for what you did to Joffrey.

488
00:47:00,740 --> 00:47:03,190
Go on-- run.

489
00:47:05,920 --> 00:47:08,640
Go! Leave! Now!

490
00:47:10,480 --> 00:47:12,930
- It's a direwolf. - I'll check down here.

491
00:47:20,360 --> 00:47:21,920
I think I heard a noise.

492
00:47:23,390 --> 00:47:24,480
Go!

493
00:47:38,740 --> 00:47:39,990
Arya!

494
00:47:41,080 --> 00:47:45,140
- Arya! - Arya!

495
00:47:45,760 --> 00:47:47,910
Arya-aa!

496
00:47:49,060 --> 00:47:50,290
Arya!

497
00:47:51,300 --> 00:47:52,790
Arya!

498
00:47:52,990 --> 00:47:54,230
My lord!

499
00:47:55,190 --> 00:47:57,430
My lord! They found her.

500
00:47:57,430 --> 00:47:58,840
She's unharmed.

501
00:47:59,920 --> 00:48:00,800
Where is she?

502
00:48:00,800 --> 00:48:02,590
She's been taken directly before the King.

503
00:48:02,590 --> 00:48:03,340
Who took her?

504
00:48:03,340 --> 00:48:04,630
The Lannisters found her.

505
00:48:04,630 --> 00:48:06,820
- Arya-aa! - Right, get back.

506
00:48:06,830 --> 00:48:09,330
The Queen ordered them to bring her straight to him.

507
00:48:09,330 --> 00:48:11,460
Back! Back to the inn.

508
00:48:12,570 --> 00:48:13,970
All back!

509
00:48:22,220 --> 00:48:24,220
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

510
00:48:24,220 --> 00:48:26,060
- Are you hurt? - No.

511
00:48:26,440 --> 00:48:28,100
Oh, it's all right.

512
00:48:29,970 --> 00:48:31,630
What is the meaning of this?

513
00:48:32,780 --> 00:48:35,270
Why was my daughter not brought to me at once?

514
00:48:35,270 --> 00:48:37,010
How dare you speak to your King in that manner?

515
00:48:37,010 --> 00:48:38,850
Quiet, woman.

516
00:48:39,540 --> 00:48:42,840
Sorry, Ned. I never meant to frighten the girl.

517
00:48:43,030 --> 00:48:45,650
But we need to get this business done quickly.

518
00:48:45,770 --> 00:48:47,240
Your girl and that butcher's boy

519
00:48:47,240 --> 00:48:48,720
attacked my son.

520
00:48:49,020 --> 00:48:51,250
That animal of hers nearly tore his arm off.

521
00:48:51,250 --> 00:48:52,920
That's not true!

522
00:48:53,130 --> 00:48:55,890
She just... Bit him a little.

523
00:48:56,580 --> 00:48:57,710
He was hurting Mycah.

524
00:48:57,720 --> 00:48:59,420
Joff told us what happened.

525
00:48:59,420 --> 00:49:01,160
You and that boy beat him with clubs

526
00:49:01,160 --> 00:49:03,920
- while you set your wolf on him. - That's not what happened!

527
00:49:03,920 --> 00:49:05,340
Yes it is!

528
00:49:05,340 --> 00:49:06,410
They all attacked me

529
00:49:06,410 --> 00:49:07,590
and she threw my sword in the river.

530
00:49:07,590 --> 00:49:08,950
- Liar! - Shut up!

531
00:49:08,950 --> 00:49:10,380
Enough!

532
00:49:10,390 --> 00:49:11,550
He tells me one thing,

533
00:49:11,550 --> 00:49:13,110
she tells me another.

534
00:49:13,400 --> 00:49:16,490
Seven hells! What am I to make of this?

535
00:49:17,910 --> 00:49:19,460
Where's your other daughter, Ned?

536
00:49:19,460 --> 00:49:20,850
In bed asleep.

537
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:22,440
She's not.

538
00:49:23,200 --> 00:49:25,550
Sansa, come here, darling.

539
00:49:36,700 --> 00:49:38,440
Now, child...

540
00:49:39,100 --> 00:49:40,960
Tell me what happened.

541
00:49:41,210 --> 00:49:43,540
Tell it all and tell it true.

542
00:49:43,540 --> 00:49:46,530
It's a great crime to lie to a King.

543
00:49:54,470 --> 00:49:56,090
I don't know.

544
00:49:56,610 --> 00:50:00,350
I don't remember. Everything happened so fast.

545
00:50:01,210 --> 00:50:03,470
- I didn't see. - Liar!

546
00:50:03,470 --> 00:50:05,130
- Liar liar liar! - Arya!

547
00:50:05,130 --> 00:50:07,580
- Hey, stop it! That's enough of that. - Liar liar liar!

548
00:50:07,580 --> 00:50:09,020
Stop! Arya!

549
00:50:09,020 --> 00:50:10,890
She's as wild as that animal of hers.

550
00:50:10,890 --> 00:50:11,870
I want her punished.

551
00:50:11,870 --> 00:50:14,950
What would you have me do, whip her through the streets?

552
00:50:14,970 --> 00:50:17,850
Damn it, children fight. It's over.

553
00:50:17,850 --> 00:50:20,560
Joffrey will bear these scars for the rest of his life.

554
00:50:21,970 --> 00:50:25,510
You let that little girl disarm you?

555
00:50:31,710 --> 00:50:34,640
Ned, see to it that your daughter is disciplined.

556
00:50:34,640 --> 00:50:36,300
I'll do the same with my son.

557
00:50:36,300 --> 00:50:37,840
Gladly, your Grace.

558
00:50:38,820 --> 00:50:40,800
And what of the direwolf?

559
00:50:41,500 --> 00:50:44,200
What of the beast that savaged your son?

560
00:50:47,320 --> 00:50:49,590
I'd forgot the damned wolf.

561
00:50:49,590 --> 00:50:52,340
We found no trace of the direwolf, your Grace.

562
00:50:52,340 --> 00:50:55,800
No? So be it.

563
00:50:55,800 --> 00:50:57,460
We have another wolf.

564
00:51:01,090 --> 00:51:02,570
As you will.

565
00:51:03,090 --> 00:51:06,210
- You can't mean it. - A direwolf's no pet.

566
00:51:06,220 --> 00:51:08,980
Get her a dog. She'll be happier for it.

567
00:51:09,720 --> 00:51:11,940
He doesn't mean Lady, does he?

568
00:51:12,250 --> 00:51:15,130
No no, not lady! Lady didn't bite anyone!

569
00:51:15,130 --> 00:51:17,550
- She's good! - Lady wasn't there!

570
00:51:17,710 --> 00:51:18,760
You leave her alone!

571
00:51:18,760 --> 00:51:20,280
Stop them. Don't let them do it.

572
00:51:20,280 --> 00:51:22,790
Please please, it wasn't Lady!

573
00:51:22,790 --> 00:51:24,570
Is this your command,

574
00:51:26,090 --> 00:51:27,820
your Grace?

575
00:51:34,120 --> 00:51:37,630
- Where is the beast? - Chained up outside, your Grace.

576
00:51:37,770 --> 00:51:39,390
Ser Ilyn, do me the honor.

577
00:51:39,390 --> 00:51:40,750
No.

578
00:51:41,930 --> 00:51:43,440
Jory...

579
00:51:45,270 --> 00:51:47,370
Take the girls to their rooms.

580
00:51:51,940 --> 00:51:53,530
If it must be done,

581
00:51:54,750 --> 00:51:56,380
then I'll do it myself.

582
00:51:56,380 --> 00:51:58,160
Is this some trick?

583
00:51:58,480 --> 00:52:00,710
The wolf is of the north.

584
00:52:01,950 --> 00:52:04,180
She deserves better than a butcher.

585
00:52:37,920 --> 00:52:39,520
The butcher's boy--

586
00:52:40,390 --> 00:52:41,890
you rode him down?

587
00:52:41,980 --> 00:52:43,360
He ran...

588
00:52:43,640 --> 00:52:45,290
Not very fast.

